        "recipient": null,
        "text": "Colonel Reba Ives does not use the title and everybody else does. She lost eleven people and a season's stock to troops flying your colors and she has been told a story about you that she is willing to hear a different version of, once, in person, because she came up in a country where a man who rides in himself is worth listening to before he is worth shooting. She is direct about what she actually wants. It is not your soldiers. It is Juan, and it is your account of the arrangement, and of those two she can only get one from you."
