        "text": "The ground is yours and it stays yours, and that is the part worth sitting with. Three claims, eleven years of work, and sixty families amounted to nothing at all the moment somebody with a state behind him decided they did. Every people on this continent that eventually gets absorbed will get absorbed for this reason and no other, and none of them will see it coming, because from the inside the absence of a government looks exactly like freedom right up until the afternoon it doesn't."
