        "text": "Mother Sabine Orr comes in person, which Brey is careful to let you understand is unusual. The hall is prepared to extend credit against next year's harvest on terms that would take your worst season off the table entirely. She would be more comfortable, she says, if your grain land stayed in grain. She says it the way a person says something obvious and pleasant, and at no point does she suggest that there is an alternative, because from where she is sitting there is not one."
