        "text": "The Croppers do not cut on the day. They are not defiant about it and they do not argue; they are simply not in the field, and not one of them can understand why this needs explaining. Their elder is a small woman named Nane Fisk who answers every question you put to her fully and courteously and does not once concede the premise. The grain is standing and the weather is turning."
