        "text": "The hall does not retaliate. It reprices. Cropper labor comes off the circuit — not banned, not denounced, simply quoted at a rate no hall between here and the river will meet — and forty years of custom ends as a line item in a schedule Chelle did not write and cannot amend. It is entirely rational and there is nobody to be angry at. Within a season they are landless, and they are landless on your ground."
